{"uid":"src/box_tree.c::bt_defer_roots","name":"bt_defer_roots","qualname":"bt_defer_roots","kind":"function","file":"src/box_tree.c","line":797,"end_line":866,"language":"c","signature":"size_t bt_defer_roots(const pv_box_def *boxes, size_t nbox, const bt_positioned *pos, size_t npos, const char *in_flow, int *root_of, size_t *order_of)","params":[{"name":"boxes","annotation":"pv_box_def *","default":"","kind":"positional"},{"name":"nbox","annotation":"size_t","default":"","kind":"positional"},{"name":"pos","annotation":"bt_positioned *","default":"","kind":"positional"},{"name":"npos","annotation":"size_t","default":"","kind":"positional"},{"name":"in_flow","annotation":"char *","default":"","kind":"positional"},{"name":"root_of","annotation":"int *","default":"","kind":"positional"},{"name":"order_of","annotation":"size_t *","default":"","kind":"positional"}],"returns":"size_t","decorators":[],"bases":[],"modifiers":[],"visibility":"public","doc":{"summary":"CSS 2.1 Appendix E steps 8-9 (spec/box_engine.md, tanda 47): an in-flow position:relative|sticky box S paints its whole subtree in the POSITIONED layer, in tree order with the absolute/fixed boxes of z-index auto/0.","description":"When one of those (an absolute backdrop, say) comes EARLIER in the tree than S, S must paint above it -- but the painter draws all in-flow content first. This names the subtrees the painter has to defer.\n\n`pos` is the positioned list (out-of-flow boxes), `in_flow[i]` nonzero when box i\nwas laid out in flow. S is deferred iff it is RELATIVE/STICKY, in flow, and some\nnon-negative-z out-of-flow P with no out-of-flow ancestor has box_index < S and\nz(P) <= z(S) (an unset z counts 0), \"earlier\" meaning TREE order (a depth-first\nwalk of the parent links: a child box can hold a lower id than its parent).\norder_of (nbox entries, may be NULL) receives that tree order so the painter can\nmerge roots with the positioned list. root_of[i] (nbox entries, always written) gets\nthe OUTERMOST deferred root that contains box i (self included) or -1. Returns\nthe number of distinct roots. Pure; bounded by nbox links per box; NULL or\nmalformed input fails OPEN: every entry -1, nothing deferred (normal paint).","params":[],"returns":null,"yields":null,"raises":[],"attributes":[],"examples":[],"notes":[["Inherited","Documentation from `bt_defer_roots` (include/box_tree.h:285)."]],"see_also":[],"deprecated":"","since":"","style":"plain"},"parent":"src/box_tree.c","members":[],"inferred_raises":[],"returns_value":null,"value":"","base_uids":[],"subclasses":[],"calls":["src/box_tree.c::bt_oof_root"],"called_by":[]}
